		summary = "**Antonio Lucio Vivaldi** (4 March 1678 – 28 July 1741) was an Italian composer, [[Virtuoso|virtuoso]] violinist and impresario of [[Baroque music]]. Regarded as one of the greatest Baroque composers, Vivaldi's influence during his lifetime was widespread across Europe, giving origin to many imitators and admirers. He pioneered many developments in [[Orchestration|orchestration]], violin technique and programmatic music. He consolidated the emerging [[Concerto|concerto]] form, especially the solo concerto, into a widely accepted and followed idiom.",
